/-! # Passing canonical Verdier evaluation through the coefficient stages -/

@[expose] public noncomputable section
set_option autoImplicit false
set_option synthInstance.maxSize 4096
universe u
open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Scheme Opposite
open scoped MonoidalCategory
namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.CondensedRing

-- Fix the site universe before inferring derived monoidal structures.
local instance (X : Scheme.{u}) : EssentiallySmall.{u + 1} X.ProEt :=
  essentiallySmallSelf.{0, u, u + 1} _

variable (Λ : Sheaf (coherentTopology Profinite.{u}) Ab.{u + 1})
  [MonObj Λ] [IsCommMonObj Λ]

/-- Integral, rational and algebraic-closure coefficients inherit invertibility
of the evaluation transpose from the finite stages.

Source: latest blueprint, det-pd-biduality-coefficients.proof.md, paragraphs (ii)--(iv).
(blueprint: lem-sf-condensed-verdier-coefficient-passage).

Proof:
1. First use the displayed ring isomorphism to reduce to the corresponding
canonical coefficient object. Exact restriction of scalars preserves finite
constant models, Tor intervals, the closed tensor structure and compact support.
Uniqueness of the constructible right adjoint identifies the dualizing objects
with their adjunction counits. Thus it identifies the canonical evaluation maps.
2. Over O_E, integral_models gives derived uniformizer completeness for K and
its double dual: both belong to the bounded constructible category by
internalHom_stability. The scalar-six exceptional and internal-Hom comparisons
identify the first reduction of evaluation with finite-coefficient evaluation.
This is invertible by condensedVerdier_finite_evaluation. The comparison with
the normalized DVR presentation carries completeness and this reduction to the
hypotheses of reduction_and_derived_nakayama. Use
embeddedIntegralCompletenessTransport and internal_completion_stacks_comparison
for the kernel-ideal/Roos completeness bridge, comparing their scalar restrictions.
Its morphism criterion makes the
original evaluation invertible.
3. For E, integral_models generates every bounded constructible complex by
finitely many cones and shifts of integral lattices extended by zero. The scalar
exceptional and internal-Hom comparisons identify evaluation on a rationalized
lattice with scalar extension of integral evaluation, including its actual map.
Hence evaluation is invertible on these generators. Native contravariant
internal-Hom exactness makes the double dual preserve distinguished triangles
up to their third map. Express K shifted by n as K tensor the shifted unit, an
invertible object. MonoidalClosed.isIso_toIhomIhom_tensor_iff gives shift
invariance of evaluation invertibility. Naturality and the four known shifted
endpoint isomorphisms satisfy Pretriangulated.isIso_app_obj₂_of_distTriang.
This criterion propagates invertibility through finite cones and shifts.
4. For the finite-subextension-valued algebraic closure, use
coefficient_finite_descent_objects for K and its duals. Take a common finite
coefficient field for these finitely many models. The finite-representative and
eventual-equality clauses of coefficient_finite_descent_hom descend the duality
maps and their finitely many identities after enlarging that field. The
scalar-six exceptional and closed comparisons identify these maps with the
specified adjoint and evaluation maps. Thus the model evaluation is the one of
case 3. Extending its isomorphism and transporting along the model isomorphism
proves invertibility for K. All transports act on evaluation itself, and the
zero object and empty scheme are included throughout. -/
theorem condensedVerdier_coefficient_passage
    (ℓ : ℕ) [Fact ℓ.Prime] (k : Type u) [Field k]
    [Fact (ringChar k).Prime] [Fact (ringChar k ≠ ℓ)]
    (hk : Finite k ∨ IsAlgClosed k) (hcd : BaseFieldFiniteCD ℓ k)
    (E : PadicAlgCl.FiniteIntermediateField ℓ)
    (he : Nonempty (Mon.mk Λ ≅ Mon.mk (Profinite.padicIntegersRingObj ℓ E.1)) ∨
      Nonempty (Mon.mk Λ ≅ Mon.mk (Profinite.continuousMapRingObj E.1)) ∨
      Nonempty (Mon.mk Λ ≅ Mon.mk (Profinite.padicAlgClRingObj ℓ)))
    (hΛ : IsLocalizingAdmissibleCoefficient ℓ Λ)
    (T : Over (Spec (.of k))) [LocallyOfFiniteType T.hom]
    [QuasiCompact T.hom] [IsSeparated T.hom]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (Over.mk (𝟙 (Spec (.of k)))).hom]
    [QuasiCompact (Over.mk (𝟙 (Spec (.of k)))).hom]
    [IsSeparated (Over.mk (𝟙 (Spec (.of k)))).hom]
    (G : ConstantModelConstructibleFiniteTor Λ (Spec (.of k)) ⥤
      ConstantModelConstructibleFiniteTor Λ T.left)
    (adj : ctfLowerShriek Λ ℓ k hcd (Over.mkIdTerminal.from T) hΛ ⊣ G)
    (N : ConstantModelConstructibleFiniteTor Λ (Spec (.of k)))
    (hN : N.obj = 𝟙_ (moduleDerived Λ (Spec (.of k)))) :
    letI := DerivedCategory.braidedCategory'.{u + 1, u + 1, u + 2}
      (Mod (Sheaf (Scheme.ProEt.topology T.left) Ab.{u + 1}) (condensedRingObj Λ T.left))
    ∀ K : moduleDerived Λ T.left, dctfPred Λ T.left K →
      IsIso (MonoidalClosed.toIhomIhom (G.obj N).obj K) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.CondensedRing
